SUSPECTED BUG: call site of retry.Do with a local closure returning ErrBusy or errDryRun (closure + Is/As guards +
double %w). Correct set: errDryRun bare (not transient: returned as is), ErrGaveUp and ErrBusy behind
"%w after %d attempts: %w", ctx.Err() behind "retry: interrupted: %w"; ErrBusy never bare, errDryRun never behind the
gave-up wrap. Actual: 125 entries, the same as the declaration of retry.Value: the closure argument does not narrow
op's Candidates (3 candidates: also Value's and Service.Transfer's closures, so NotFoundError, filerepo and tx
errors appear; plan S09 is not implemented). errDryRun behind the gave-up wrap is the documented dominance
over-approximation of tx_ping_decl and not part of the suspected bug.
-- args --
-fanout=1 cmd/cli/main.go:@retry_busy_call
